0.152\n\n0.821\n\n0.223\n\n0.451\n\n0.092\n\n0.156\n\n0.209\n\n0.980\n\n0.016\n\n0.003\n\n0.345\n\n0.262\n\n0.911\n\n0.001\n\n0.042\n\n0.411\n\n0.226\n\n0.238\n\n0.265\n\n0.702\n\n0.397\n\np-value*\n\n0.156\n\n0.380\n\n0.555\n\n0.036\n\n0.047\n\n0.816\n\nTable 5. Comparative analysis of baseline characteristics of kidney transplant recipients with and without\n\nSARS-CoV-2 specific T cell immunity response after two doses of inactivated vaccine. Results are expressed\n\nas median (interquartile range) and number (%). Continuous data were compared using the Mann-Whitney\n\nU-test, and categorical variables with the chi-square. KTRs kidney transplant recipients, MMF mycophenolate mofetil, ATG anti-thymocyte globulin. *p-value of Univariate analysis. *p-value of Multiple logistic regression\n\nanalyses.\n\nRecent data indicated the third homologues booster with inactivated vaccine could not further increase the cellular immunity against SARS-CoV-2'º. However, third booster with mRNA vaccine or adenovirus vector\n\nvaccine could further increase the SARS-CoV-2 specific T cells in healthy individuals vaccinated with two doses\n\nof inactivated vaccine®,24. Thus, a third dose with heterologous vaccine might be a better strategy for improving\n\nT cell immunity response in these patients7,27\n\nStudies, including our own, have demonstrated that there is a discordance between the humoral and cellular\n\nimmunity response after SARS-CoV-2 vaccination in KTRs4. This discordance may be due to the immunosup\n\npressive drugs these patients are on. The triple immunosuppression regime significantly disturbs the interaction\n\nbetween T follicular helper (Tfh) cells and B cells in the germinal center, and suppresses the proliferation of activated T and B cells4445. These processes are pivotal to anti-SARS-CoV-2 specific antibody generation 18,46,47\n\nIn contrast to our study, Bruminhent et al. have shown that the spike and NP specific T cells were enhanced in healthy people after two doses of inactivated vaccine, but not in KTRs'. They reported that in KTRs the sum\n\nof T cells against spike and NP was 58 SFU/10° PBMCs after two doses of inactivated vaccine. This was lower\n\nthan that reported in our study (median SFU/10° PBMCs against spike: 67.5, median SFU/10° PBMCs against\n\nScientific Reports | (2023) 13:7263 | https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-29669-8\n\nnature portfolio", "width": 2174, "height": 1654, "blocks": [{"kind": "text", "text": "www.nature.com/scientificreports/", "bbox": {"x": 2107.0, "y": 110.3, "width": 31.90000000000009, "height": 448.59999999999997}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Female sex", "bbox": {"x": 1956.0, "y": 119.9, "width": 19.0, "height": 91.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Age(year)", "bbox": {"x": 1921.2, "y": 119.9, "width": 19.0, "height": 82.1}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Body mass index", "bbox": {"x": 1889.6, "y": 119.9, "width": 19.0, "height": 138.9}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "White blood cell (× 109)", "bbox": {"x": 1858.0, "y": 119.9, "width": 19.0, "height": 189.4}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Lymphocyte(× 10°)", "bbox": {"x": 1823.3, "y": 119.9, "width": 22.09999999999991, "height": 154.70000000000002}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Platelet (× 10')", "bbox": {"x": 1791.7, "y": 119.9, "width": 19.0, "height": 119.9}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Hemoglobin (g/L)", "bbox": {"x": 1756.9, "y": 119.9, "width": 22.09999999999991, "height": 148.4}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Creatinine (umol/L)", "bbox": {"x": 1723.8, "y": 122.7, "width": 23.90000000000009, "height": 161.7}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Alanine aminotransferase (U/L)", "bbox": {"x": 1696.9, "y": 119.9, "width": 19.0, "height": 252.49999999999997}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Aspartate aminotransferase (U/L)", "bbox": {"x": 1662.1, "y": 119.9, "width": 19.0, "height": 265.1}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Total bilirubin (umol/L)", "bbox": {"x": 1627.3, "y": 119.9, "width": 22.09999999999991, "height": 195.70000000000002}}, {"kind": "text", "text